    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-speaking-3', 41, 'Listen & Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-06-extra-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clarification meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう一度言っていただけますか？”.","hintJa":"聞き返す丁寧な表現。","explanation":"Model: “Could you say that again?” (もう一度言っていただけますか？). Connect the complete message naturally; the second attempt checks independent recall.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Could you say that again?」（もう一度言っていただけますか？）です。文全体を自然につなげ、2回目は見ずに思い出して言いましょう。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try once more without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Could you say that again?","speakJa":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-speaking-4', 42, 'Listen & Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-06-extra-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"experience","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the experience meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “それは今まで試したことがありません。”.","hintJa":"現在完了の経験。","explanation":"Model: “I’ve never tried that before.” (それは今まで試したことがありません。). Connect the complete message naturally; the second attempt checks independent recall.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’ve never tried that before.」（それは今まで試したことがありません。）です。文全体を自然につなげ、2回目は見ずに思い出して言いましょう。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try once more without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’ve never tried that before.","speakJa":"それは今まで試したことがありません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-speaking-5', 43, 'Listen & Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-06-extra-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Listen & Speak","topic":"learning","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the learning meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そこが難しいと感じる部分です。”.","hintJa":"苦手な箇所を説明する。","explanation":"Model: “That’s the part I find difficult.” (そこが難しいと感じる部分です。). Connect the complete message naturally; the second attempt checks independent recall.","explanationJa":"お手本は「That’s the part I find difficult.」（そこが難しいと感じる部分です。）です。文全体を自然につなげ、2回目は見ずに思い出して言いましょう。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try once more without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"That’s the part I find difficult.","speakJa":"そこが難しいと感じる部分です。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-visual-1', 51, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-06-extra-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A learner politely asks a speaker to repeat what was said. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「もう一度言っていただけますか？」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A learner politely asks a speaker to repeat what was said. That directly matches “Could you say that again?” (もう一度言っていただけますか？); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「もう一度言っていただけますか？」という場面を表しています。そのため「Could you say that again?」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Could you say that again?","jp":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"What do you mean?","jp":"どういう意味ですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Can you give me an example?","jp":"例を一つ教えてもらえますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s the part I find difficult.","jp":"そこが難しいと感じる部分です。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-06-01-say-again.webp","imageAlt":"A learner politely asks a speaker to repeat what was said.","visualAssetId":"july-06-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-visual-2', 52, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-06-extra-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"change","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A commuter becomes more comfortable using a crowded train over time. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「だんだん慣れてきました。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A commuter becomes more comfortable using a crowded train over time. That directly matches “I’m getting used to it.” (だんだん慣れてきました。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「だんだん慣れてきました。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’m getting used to it.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m getting used to it.","jp":"だんだん慣れてきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve never tried that before.","jp":"それは今まで試したことがありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"It was better than I expected.","jp":"思っていたより良かったです。"},{"id":"d","en":"That’s the part I find difficult.","jp":"そこが難しいと感じる部分です。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-06-02-getting-used-to-it.webp","imageAlt":"A commuter becomes more comfortable using a crowded train over time.","visualAssetId":"july-06-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-visual-3', 53, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-06-extra-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"experience","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A beginner hesitantly tries pottery for the first time. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「それは今まで試したことがありません。」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A beginner hesitantly tries pottery for the first time. That directly matches “I’ve never tried that before.” (それは今まで試したことがありません。); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「それは今まで試したことがありません。」という場面を表しています。そのため「I’ve never tried that before.」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve never tried that before.","jp":"それは今まで試したことがありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m getting used to it.","jp":"だんだん慣れてきました。"},{"id":"c","en":"It was better than I expected.","jp":"思っていたより良かったです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ll check and let you know.","jp":"確認してお知らせします。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-06-03-never-tried-before.webp","imageAlt":"A beginner hesitantly tries pottery for the first time.","visualAssetId":"july-06-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
    ('july-06', 'july-06-extra-visual-4', 54, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-06-extra-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"learning","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Use the visible action and objects as evidence: A learner asks a teacher to demonstrate one concrete example. Choose the sentence that describes the complete scene.","hintJa":"人物の動作や物を確認し、「例を一つ教えてもらえますか？」に合う場面か考えましょう。見えている場面全体を説明する英文を選んでください。","explanation":"The illustration shows this scene: A learner asks a teacher to demonstrate one concrete example. That directly matches “Can you give me an example?” (例を一つ教えてもらえますか？); the other choices describe different actions or situations.","explanationJa":"人物の動作や物が「例を一つ教えてもらえますか？」という場面を表しています。そのため「Can you give me an example?」が一致し、他の選択肢は別の動作・場面です。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Can you give me an example?","jp":"例を一つ教えてもらえますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Could you say that again?","jp":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"What do you mean?","jp":"どういう意味ですか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ll check and let you know.","jp":"確認してお知らせします。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-06-04-give-example.webp","imageAlt":"A learner asks a teacher to demonstrate one concrete example.","visualAssetId":"july-06-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
